<section class="hero" style="padding-bottom: 1rem;">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="eyebrow">how we work</span>
    <h1 style="max-width: 14ch;">A process that doesn't end at launch<span class="hero__cursor"></span></h1>
    <p class="hero__sub">Most agency processes stop at delivery. Ours has a fifth step for a reason — that's where the dedicated-assistant model actually kicks in.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-border-top">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 760px;">
    <div class="process-step reveal">
      <div class="process-step__num">01</div>
      <div>
        <h3>Discovery call</h3>
        <p>We talk through what you're trying to build, grow, or support — no pitch deck, just questions specific to your project. This usually surfaces which of our four service areas actually apply.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="process-step reveal">
      <div class="process-step__num">02</div>
      <div>
        <h3>Scope & proposal</h3>
        <p>We come back with a concrete scope, timeline, and pricing model — fixed-scope, retainer, or staff augmentation, whichever fits the project. No vague "let's discuss further" loops.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="process-step reveal">
      <div class="process-step__num">03</div>
      <div>
        <h3>Design & architecture</h3>
        <p>For builds, this means data modeling and system design before any code. For marketing, it means positioning and channel strategy before any campaign spend. We don't skip this step to look faster.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="process-step reveal">
      <div class="process-step__num">04</div>
      <div>
        <h3>Build & launch</h3>
        <p>Regular check-ins, not a black-box build followed by a surprise reveal. You'll see progress throughout, not just at the end.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="process-step reveal">
      <div class="process-step__num">05</div>
      <div>
        <h3>Managed support</h3>
        <p>Once live, you're handed to a dedicated assistant who already has full context on the project — for ongoing updates, fixes, and small requests, without re-explaining everything to someone new.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

